WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.601
-Also happening next week,
I have a new children's book

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.167
coming out on Tuesday called
"Con Pollo."

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:07.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.100
I wrote it with Jennifer Lopez.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.901
It's a fun this-or-that book
that helps you

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.534
teach your kids
how to speak Spanish.

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:18.467
-[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.767
-Oh, my --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.534
Rosita -- Rosita,
what are you doing here?

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.133
Why are you not on
"Sesame Street"?

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:28.467
-Oh, Jimmy, you have a new look.
-I do.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.434
-Yeah, you're starting to look
like you're Pancho.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:33.200
The monster in you
is coming out.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.901
-It's coming out.
I'm getting furry. Yeah.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.200
-But you know what?

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.567
I heard about your new book,

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.601
and yo hablo Español --
I speak Spanish.

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:41.934
I'm so excited.

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:43.667
And I'm learning
how to read, Jimmy.

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.133
And my favorite part about
reading -- you know what it is?

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:47.367
-No.

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.067
-Finding out what happens
at the end of the book.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.801
So, tell me, what happens at
the end of your book?

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:53.834
-Well, it's not really about
the end of the book.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:56.133
-Yes, please. Por favor.

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:58.801
-Yeah, but it's more about
the journey that you take.

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:00.734
-Sure, sure, sure.
Okay, yeah. Mm-hmm.

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.934
-But, like,
do you want to go to the beach

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.968
or do you want to go to
la playa?

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.434
-Ooh, la playa.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:07.734
But how does it end?

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.801
Tell me. How does it end?
Yeah, mm-hmm.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:12.400
So exciting! Jimmy, come on!

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.100
-Do you want to play
soccer or play fútbol?

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.634
-Oh, she's so cute.
Look at that.

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:19.601
Look at that pollito lindo.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:20.868
-Yeah, yeah,
but how does it end?

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:21.901
How does it end?

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:25.634
-Do you want to go to school

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.267
or do you want to go to
la escuela?

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:28.601
-La escuela.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:32.501
Jimmy, Jimmy, look at
the escuela with the campana.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:33.868
-Yeah.
-With the backpack.

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.200
Jimmy...
-Yes?

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.501
-...do you know where
I really want to go right now?

00:01:37.501 --> 00:01:38.634
-Where?

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.567
-To the end of the book,
por favor!

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.100
I'm so excited!
-Alright, alright.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.567
The end of the book says,
"Let's say good night.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.200
Tomorrow's another day."

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.868
You can read this again.
-Let me see.

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:51.434
-This time, pollito will play.

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:54.534
-Aww! Pollito!

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:56.534
-Pollito! It's cute.
-So cute.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.667
-And that's the end.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.234
Then you can finally see
the end is --

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:01.267
-Let me see. Let me see.
Ah, the end.

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.334
-Fin -- the end.
That's it right there, yes.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:04.667
-Oh, Jimmy!

00:02:04.667 --> 00:02:05.934
-Thank you for
helping me, Rosita.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:08.100
-Oh, I love you so much.
Can I take it home?

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:09.400
-Yes, of course
you can take it home.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.434
-And can you please read it
to me later on, again?

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:12.734
The whole thing?

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.901
-I will FaceTime you tonight
and read you a book.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.567
-Okay, at what time?

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.234
Because I have to go to bed
at 8:00.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:19.868
-I know.
Already, it's past your bedtime.

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.868
-I know. What am I doing here?
-What are you doing here?

00:02:21.868 --> 00:02:22.934
-Oh, my goodness!

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:24.033
-You have to get back to
"Sesame Street."

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.133
-Yes, I have to --
You know what?

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:26.334
The count says hello.

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:28.400
It took him forever
to say goodbye.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.000
I mean,
to say hello and goodbye.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.634
So I just run out.
So I'm going to go now.

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.734
-You're going to go? Bye.
Rosita, so great to see you.

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:35.734
And thank you. You can come by
whenever you like.

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:37.667
-Oh, thank you.
Can I take two markers?

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.334
Let me put my book down here.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.968
I need some markers.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.534
-You want these markers?

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:45.501
-Yeah, and I think
I need a new microphone.

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:46.634
But I'm going to leave it there,

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.033
because I don't have
any more hands.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.434
So can I come back later
for the microphone?

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:53.167
-Yes.
-And Elmito wants some gear.

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.601
Do you have anything there?
-My mug?

00:02:57.601 --> 00:02:59.067
-Yeah, but it has --
No, never mind.

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:00.968
Okay, I'm going to go.
-You can take --

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.734
-But...

00:03:02.734 --> 00:03:04.033
-I have nothing else
to give you.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:05.501
-I'm going to go down
the stairs now.

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:06.801
-You're going to go down
the stairs. Bye.

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.901
-I love you.
-I love you, too. Bye.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.167
Oh.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.434
-iAdios!

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:19.133
♪♪

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:21.601
-Aww! I got
a cute kiss from Rosita.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.834
Come on.

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.767
Guys, "Sesame Street's"
53rd season

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:29.100
debuts November 3rd
on Cartoonito on HBO Max.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:31.801
Bye, Rosita!

